## Style Rules (MANDATORY)

1. **No `from __future__ import annotations`** - Python 3.13 has `X | None` natively; Pydantic{% if not mongo and not nodb %} and SQLAlchemy{% endif %} read annotations at runtime, and the future import makes ruff (TC rules) move runtime-needed imports into `TYPE_CHECKING`. Quote forward references instead ({% if mongo or nodb %}`list["Task"]`{% else %}`Mapped[list["Task"]]`{% endif %})
2. **Type annotations** - On all function parameters and return types
3. **Google-style docstrings** - On all public classes and functions
4. **PEP 8** - Enforced by Ruff (line length 88)
5. **f-strings** - For all string formatting
6. **`snake_case`** - For functions, methods, variables
7. **`PascalCase`** - For classes
8. **`str | None`** - Union syntax (not `Optional[str]`)
9. **`list[X]`, `dict[K, V]`** - Lowercase generics (not `typing.List`)
10. **`model_dump()`** - Never use deprecated `.dict()`
{% if nodb %}
11. **No ORM** - Pydantic models or dataclasses; no database layer unless the task asks for one
{% elif mongo %}
11. **`ObjectId`** - Convert ids at the service boundary; never put a raw `ObjectId` in a response schema
{% else %}
11. **`Mapped[]`** - For all SQLAlchemy column types
{% endif %}
12. **`async def`** - For {% if nodb %}async I/O (not for pure computation){% else %}all I/O operations{% endif %}

